  "answer_text": "Because **\"Glenwood Pool\"** can refer to several different well-known pools and swim clubs across the United States, here is a guide to the most popular locations to help you find the right one:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" in the world, renowned as the **world's largest natural hot springs pool**. \n* **The Experience:** Heated by the geothermal Yampah Spring (meaning \"Big Medicine\" in the Ute language), the water contains 15 naturally occurring therapeutic minerals. \n* **Pools & Attractions:**\n  * **The Grand Pool:** A massive pool spanning over two city blocks, kept at a comfortable 90\u00b0F (32\u00b0C).\n  * **The Therapy Pool:** A hotter, more relaxing soaking pool kept at 104\u00b0F (40\u00b0C).\n  * **Yampah Mineral Baths:** A collection of five natural, serene mineral pools designed primarily for adults.\n  * **Sopris Splash Zone:** A family-friendly area featuring water slides (the Shoshone Chutes adventure river ride) and a splash pad.\n* **Admission:** Daily pool passes typically range from **$38 to $55** depending on the day and season. Lodging at the resort includes unlimited pool access.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Glenwood Pool (Silver Spring, Maryland)\nA highly popular private community swim club nestled in a historic, wooded neighborhood.\n* **The Experience:** Set back among the trees and along a creek in historic Forest Glen, MD, it has a tight-knit community vibe.\n* **Features:** It hosts a neighborhood swim team, social events, and recreational swimming.\n* **Membership:** Access requires a seasonal membership. Because of its popularity, there is often a waitlist, and new members pay a one-time, non-refundable initiation fee (historically around $700) along with annual dues.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Glenwood Pool (Columbus, Ohio)\nA public community pool operated by the **Columbus Recreation and Parks Department**.\n* **The Experience:** A family-friendly, public outdoor neighborhood pool.\n* **Access:** Admission is very affordable, but guests must obtain a free Columbus Recreation and Parks **Leisure Card** in advance to enter. \n* **Season:** It generally opens for the summer season around Memorial Day weekend and operates through mid-to-late August. \n\n---\n\n### 4. Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia)\nLocated in the Glenwood Park neighborhood of Atlanta.\n* **The Experience:** A private, junior Olympic-sized, 6-lane **saline pool**.\n* **Features:** It includes a fitness center (open year-round), an adjacent kids' water play area, and picnic grounds. \n* **Membership:** Open to neighborhood residents and outside members via a waitlist system.\n\n***\n\n*If you are looking for specific details (like hours, directions, or membership pricing) for one of these pools, please let me know which location you are interested in!*",
